      "side": 1,
      "message": "An incompatible change like this needs to duplicate the struct to a _v2 struct and keep the original struct as _v1. The relevant code needs to handle both formats. Otherwise, it will break the existing devices which use the v1 struct. The complication may not justified.\n\nAn easier way is to create a new CMD for these new operations, like `EC_CMD_READ_CROS_BOARD_INFO`/`EC_CMD_WRITE_CROS_BOARD_INFO` instead of overloading the `EC_CMD_GET_CROS_BOARD_INFO`/`EC_CMD_SET_CROS_BOARD_INFO`.\n\nYou can check the above `EC_CMD_FLASH_READ`/`EC_CMD_FLASH_WRITE`. The params should be similar.",
